d-style=&quot;font-family: &amp;quot;Google Sans&amp;quot;, Arial, sans-serif, &amp;quot;Noto Color Emoji&amp;quot;; font-size: 16px; font-weight: 400; margin: 0px; text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 0px rgb(10, 10, 10);&quot; data-complete=&quot;true&quot; data-sfc-root=&quot;ep&quot; data-sfc-cp=&quot;&quot; class=&quot;iNqyIf&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 700; margin: 0px; border-bottom: 0px rgb(10, 10, 10);&quot; data-copy-service-computed-style=&quot;font-family: &amp;quot;Google Sans&amp;quot;, Arial, sans-serif, &amp;quot;Noto Color Emoji&amp;quot;; font-size: 16px; font-weight: 700; margin: 0px; text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 0px rgb(10, 10, 10);&quot; data-complete=&quot;true&quot; data-sfc-root=&quot;ep&quot; data-sfc-cp=&quot;&quot; class=&quot;rQesXe MPyX&quot;&gt;Local vs. Distributed Consistency:&lt;/span&gt; The write side (Commands) often relies on local &lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 700; margin: 0px; border-bottom: 0px rgb(10, 10, 10);&quot; data-copy-service-computed-style=&quot;font-family: &amp;quot;Google Sans&amp;quot;, Arial, sans-serif, &amp;quot;Noto Color Emoji&amp;quot;; font-size: 16px; font-weight: 700; margin: 0px; text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 0px rgb(10, 10, 10);&quot; data-complete=&quot;true&quot; data-sfc-root=&quot;ep&quot; data-sfc-cp=&quot;&quot; class=&quot;rQesXe MPyX&quot;&gt;ACID transactions&lt;/span&gt; to ensure integrity when modifying state.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;margin: 0px; border-bottom: 0px rgb(10, 10, 10);&quot; data-copy-service-computed-style=&quot;font-family: &amp;quot;Google Sans&amp;quot;, Arial, sans-serif, &amp;quot;Noto Color Emoji&amp;quot;; font-size: 16px; font-weight: 400; margin: 0px; text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 0px rgb(10, 10, 10);&quot; data-complete=&quot;true&quot; data-hveid=&quot;CAIIAAgACCEQAw&quot; data-ved=&quot;2ahUKEwjC7Zm93fyWAxWKleEIHfdwJKAQi4wTegoIAggACAAIIRAD&quot; data-sfc-root=&quot;ep&quot; data-sfc-cp=&quot;&quot; class=&quot;&quot; data-bfc=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;margin: 0px 0px 12px; border-bottom: 0px rgb(10, 10, 10);&quot; data-copy-service-computed-style=&quot;font-family: &amp;quot;Google Sans&amp;quot;, Arial, sans-serif, &amp;quot;Noto Color Emoji&amp;quot;; font-size: 16px; font-weight: 400; margin: 0px 0px 12px; text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 0px rgb(10, 10, 10);&quot; data-complete=&quot;true&quot; data-hveid=&quot;CAIIAAgACCEQBA&quot; data-sfc-root=&quot;ep&quot; data-sfc-cp=&quot;&quot; class=&quot;Z1qcYe&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;margin: 0px; border-bottom: 0px rgb(10, 10, 10);&quot; data-copy-service-computed-style=&quot;font-family: &amp;quot;Google Sans&amp;quot;, Arial, sans-serif, &amp;quot;Noto Color Emoji&amp;quot;; font-size: 16px; font-weight: 400; margin: 0px; text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 0px rgb(10, 10, 10);&quot; data-complete=&quot;true&quot; data-sfc-root=&quot;ep&quot; data-sfc-cp=&quot;&quot; class=&quot;iNqyIf&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 700; margin: 0px; border-bottom: 0px rgb(10, 10, 10);&quot; data-copy-service-computed-style=&quot;font-family: &amp;quot;Google Sans&amp;quot;, Arial, sans-serif, &amp;quot;Noto Color Emoji&amp;quot;; font-size: 16px; font-weight: 700; margin: 0px; text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 0px rgb(10, 10, 10);&quot; data-complete=&quot;true&quot; data-sfc-root=&quot;ep&quot; data-sfc-cp=&quot;&quot; class=&quot;rQesXe MPyX&quot;&gt;Eventual Consistency:&lt;/span&gt; When CQRS splits into separate physical read and write databases, data replication is usually asynchronous. This means the overall system trades strict global ACID guarantees for &lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 700; margin: 0px; border-bottom: 0px rgb(10, 10, 10);&quot; data-copy-service-computed-style=&quot;font-family: &amp;quot;Google Sans&amp;quot;, Arial, sans-serif, &amp;quot;Noto Color Emoji&amp;quot;; font-size: 16px; font-weight: 700; margin: 0px; text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 0px rgb(10, 10, 10);&quot; data-complete=&quot;true&quot; data-sfc-root=&quot;ep&quot; data-sfc-cp=&quot;&quot; class=&quot;rQesXe MPyX&quot;&gt;eventual consistency&lt;/span&gt; across the read models.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;overflow=hidden;rounded=0;fontSize=15;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="20" y="10" width="810" height="730" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
  <diagram id="nJDaHy2LMW60uCfPk2dV" name="SOLID">
    <mxGraphModel dx="1096" dy="662" grid="1" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="850" pageHeight="1100" math="0" shadow="0">
      <root>
        <mxCell id="0" />
        <mxCell id="1" parent="0" />
        <mxCell id="xgdkxCzUxtXAjiak5gKo-1" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;overflow=hidden;rounded=0;fontSize=20;" value="&lt;h1 style=&quot;margin-top: 0px;&quot;&gt;SOLID&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;div&gt;SRP - Single responsibility principle - I will create capabalities that can be segregated as separate classes&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;OCP - A class or method is open for extension closed for modification&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Linkovs principle - A child should be able to substitute the parent without breaking the functionality&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; If a piece of code expects a Parent, handing it a Child should not break anything.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;ISP - Interface segregation principle - use multiple capabalities defined as interface so that there is effective way of creating capabalities in the implementation class&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Dependency Injection - Dependency should be externalized and supplied to the method/implementation wanting to use it, rather than instantiating it&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;```&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&amp;lt;!DOCTYPE html&amp;gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&amp;lt;html lang=&quot;en&quot;&amp;gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&amp;lt;head&amp;gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;lt;meta charset=&quot;UTF-8&quot;&amp;gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;lt;title&amp;gt;Minimal SOLID Web App&amp;lt;/title&amp;gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;lt;style&amp;gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; body { font-family: sans-serif; margin: 40px; max-width: 600px; line-height: 1.6; }&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; .box { border: 1px solid #ccc; padding: 15px; margin: 15px 0; border-radius: 5px; }&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; .good { background-color: #e6f4ea; border-color: #34a853; }&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; .bad { background-color: #fce8e6; border-color: #ea4335; }&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;lt;/style&amp;gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&amp;lt;/head&amp;gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&amp;lt;body&amp;gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;lt;h2&amp;gt;SOLID Principles Demo&amp;lt;/h2&amp;gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;lt;div class=&quot;box bad&quot;&amp;gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;lt;h3&amp;gt;Bad (Non-SOLID) Output&amp;lt;/h3&amp;gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;lt;div id=&quot;bad-output&quot;&amp;gt;&amp;lt;/div&amp;gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;lt;/div&amp;gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;lt;div class=&quot;box good&quot;&amp;gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;lt;h3&amp;gt;Good (SOLID) Output&amp;lt;/h3&amp;gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;lt;div id=&quot;good-output&quot;&amp;gt;&amp;lt;/div&amp;gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;lt;/div&amp;gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;lt;script&amp;gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; // ==========================================&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; // ❌ THE BAD WAY (Violates SOLID)&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; // ==========================================&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; // Violates SRP: Handles both data and rendering.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; // Violates OCP: If we add a &#39;Circle&#39;, we must modify this class&#39;s inner logic.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; class BadAreaCalculator {&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; constructor(width, height) {&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; this.width = width;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; this.height = height;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; }&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; renderResult() {&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; const area = this.width * this.height;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; document.getElementById(&#39;bad-output&#39;).innerText = `Rectangle Area: ${area}`;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; }&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; }&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; // Run Bad Demo&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; const badCalc = new BadAreaCalculator(10, 5);&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; badCalc.renderResult();&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; // ==========================================&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; //&amp;nbsp; THE GOOD WAY (Follows SOLID)&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; // ==========================================&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; // [S] Single Responsibility: This class ONLY calculates, it doesn&#39;t touch the DOM.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; // [O] Open/Closed: Open to extension (new shapes), closed to modification.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; // [L] Liskov Substitution: Any shape subclass can replace &#39;Shape&#39; without breaking code.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; class Shape {&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; getArea() { throw new Error(&quot;Method must be implemented&quot;); }&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; }&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; class Rectangle extends Shape {&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; constructor(width, height) {&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; super();&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; this.width = width;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; this.height = height;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; }&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; getArea() { return this.width * this.height; }&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; }&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; // [I] Interface Segregation: Handled inherently (JavaScript doesn&#39;t force unused methods).&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; // [D] Dependency Inversion: Renderer depends on the abstract &#39;Shape&#39;, not the concrete &#39;Rectangle&#39;.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; class DomRenderer {&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; static display(elementId, shape) {&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; document.getElementById(elementId).innerText = `Calculated Area: ${shape.getArea()}`;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; }&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; }&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; // Run Good Demo&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; const myRectangle = new Rectangle(10, 5);&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; DomRenderer.display(&#39;good-output&#39;, myRectangle);&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;lt;/script&amp;gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&amp;lt;/body&amp;gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&amp;lt;/html&amp;gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;```&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="2500" width="830" x="10" y="10" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
</mxfile>
